it's been more than a decade since  hotshot rookie racer lightning McQueen  burst onto the big screen in the first  Cars movie now he's back in cars three  with the cast of new characters as well  as old favorites to get his life back on  track  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers it's Jan here  and in this video I'm going to uncover  some amazing secrets and facts about the  making of Pixar's latest animated movie  I'm also running my special cars three  giveaway on this video as well for a  chance to be one of two lucky people  who'll win this very cool the art of  cars three hardback book featuring  Pixar's fabulous concept art storyboards  and insights into the movie all you need  to do is subscribe and leave a comment  about the film and also answer the  question I'll be asking later in the  video many years of work go into each of  Pixar's animated features and naturally  over the course of those years  screenplays and character designs go  through numerous changes in fact during  the production of cars three artists  created over 80,000 storyboards for the  film however only around ten thousand of  those made it into the final movie but  thankfully sometimes the animators on a  new movie can make use of the good work  done by their colleagues on a previous  Pixar film for example when you look at  the sky in cars three 85% of those  clouds you see actually came from the  cloud library for the good dinosaur  although sadly screen legend Paul Newman  died back in 2008 his cars character Doc  Hudson still plays a crucial part in the  new movie and doc is voiced once again  by Newman himself thanks to many hours  of conversations between the renowned  actor and Cars director John Lasseter  there were caught on tape during voice  recording sessions for the first movie a  lot of what Paul Newman and John  Lasseter talked about between takes was  racing related so when the filmmakers  trawled through those recordings looking  for material that would work for cars  three they had a veritable treasure  trove of dialogue to choose from when  the animators were working out how  lightning McQueen's face should move  they look to Owen Wilson the voice actor  behind the car for inspiration which  means that the way lightning mooses  mouth in the movie is based on the shape  of Owen Wilson's mouth when he talks  including the way the actor curls and  purses his lips the movie's design team  wanted the look of next gen racer  Jackson storm to be incomplete  contrast the look of Lightning McQueen  so they went for a sharp angular design  for Jackson which stands out compared to  lightnings more rounded flowing look in  fact Jackson's storm is actually how the  Pixar team think a stock car racer will  look 20 years from now as for the S  symbol on Jackson's side that's based on  the International hurricane symbol which  has been tweaked stretched and color  matched to give him a sleek and bold  look and to contrast with a lightning  bolt on number 95 for the appearance of  school bus miss fritter the filmmakers  took a subtle style cue from oranges any  black star Lea delaria who voices a  demolition derby champ yes just look at  miss fritters face and you'll notice  that the animators increase the thick  rubber trim around her windshield  in a hat tip to de la Rio's trademark  thick rimmed glasses on top of that miss  fretted smokestacks are another cool  easter egg as their design is based on  the horns of the classic Disney  character Maleficent who featured in the  1959 animation Sleeping Beauty as well  as the 2014 live-action movie starring  Angelina Jolie by the way for more  awesome Easter eggs and cars 3 tap the  top right of the screen to check out my  video on that when it came to bringing  to life the movie's crazy demolition  derby with all its mud and dust flying  everywhere  the filmmakers discovered how difficult  it was to make computer animated mud  that was the right consistency so it  looked realistic but didn't totally  cover up the characters to give you an  idea of just how big a task this was for  the artists and technicians working on  cars 3 there are actually 616 shots in  the movie that feature merged splatters  sand dust and dirt one of the things the  filmmakers did to ensure they got the  right design and feel for the scene  overall was to visit a night race on a  dirt track after that it was a matter of  trial and error to get the mud looking  less like cake icing or liquid chocolate  which is how it looked in early tests a  more like the combination of chunky  oatmeal and soup that director Brian fee  wanted when cars 3 production designer  JC ster joined Pixar back in the early  2000s one of the first things he had to  do was design a pay phone that could  function for a large mechanical object  that had no hands like a car Schuster's  payphone design ended up being cut from  the first Cars movie however in a little  nod to the production designer the pay  phone has been reintroduce  in cars three so remember to look out  for it during the scene at Flo's v-eight  café a chance encounter with a vintage  car rally during a meeting that the Cars  3 team had away from their Pixar offices  gave the filmmakers the idea to pay  tribute to the history of racing and  early NASCAR races in their movie among  the characters in the film based on  real-life NASCAR legends is Louise  Barnstormer Nash who is named after the  first lady of racing Louise Smith who  won 38 races in the 1940s and 50s and  who's Nash ambassador Karl ends its  number 94 to her cars three counterpart  NASCAR legend Wendell Scott who was the  first African American to win in the  grand national series also inspired the  cars three team to create a new  character called river Scott who races  under number 34 just like Wendell Scott  did also doc Hudson's old coach and  friend smokey who Lightning McQueen  turns to for help in his own career is  based on real-life racing legend the  innovative mechanic Henri smokey eunuch  who just like his namesake in the movie  ran an automobile repair shop that he  dubbed the best damn garage in town Owen  to emphasize the bond in the movie  between smokey and Doc Hudson he was a  Hudson Hornet the animators based smoked  his design on a Hudson pickup truck now  what was your favorite moment in cars 3  and who's your favorite character in the  cars movies for a chance to win this  awesome the art of car 3 hardback book  be sure to subscribe and leave a comment  about the movie and also answer the  following question which Disney  character is most fritters design a  reference to make sure you turn on your  notifications to get all my new cars 3  and Pixar videos and I'll be announcing  the winners for the giveaway on an  upcoming video congratulations to these  two winners of my recent alien covenant  giveaway if you're one of them send me a  message on youtube or via my email which  you can find on my about page so I can  get your details to send you the prize  if you enjoyed this I really appreciate  you hitting the thumbs up button and  check out some more of my Pixar a movie  secrets videos right here thanks for  watching and see you next time  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers
 

